Keep rewards, choices and combat challenges closer across different routes and decisions on the same seed. Designed for everyday play and same-seed competitions.

For example, reshuffling an extra time in one fight no longer changes the next fight’s opening hand by itself.

[b]Requirements[/b]

[list]
[*]Windows and StS2 v0.113.1 (build d09d48e5) on public-beta.
[*]Standard and Dread single-player runs only. Multiplayer, Blitz and custom modifiers are unsupported.
[*]Subscribe, enable Seedline in the game’s mod list, and start a new run.
[*]Disable Catfood, CardAscension and Combat Solver before playing.
[/list]

[b]Q&A[/b]

[b]Does this guarantee identical outcomes?[/b]
No. Your choices still affect results. Seedline reduces changes caused by unrelated actions.

[b]Does it change vanilla probabilities?[/b]
Yes. Some reward probabilities change, along with how actions affect later random outcomes.

[b]Can I save and reload?[/b]
Yes, but some outcomes that previously changed when you tried different actions will no longer reroll.

[b]Do I need everything unlocked?[/b]
No. New runs have fully unlocked content without changing your profile unlocks or Ascension limits.

[b]Are other mods required?[/b]
No. RitsuLib is optional.

[b]Does it work with modded characters?[/b]
Partially. Their shuffles, random card selections and other combat effects may retain their original behavior.

[b]Can I update or disable it mid-run?[/b]
Keep the game version, Seedline and RitsuLib setup fixed during a run. Continuing with Seedline disabled can discard its saved state. Start a new run after incompatible updates.

[b]Where can I report a problem?[/b]
Use this item’s [b]Bug Reports & Feedback[/b] discussion. Include versions, enabled mods, seed, reproduction steps and relevant logs or screenshots.
